# Lorehold Charm, first mode: Bot2's Clue is a token artifact and so is no nontoken artifact: with only that, Bot2 sacrifices
# nothing (first charm). Bot2 then plays Ornithopter, its only nontoken artifact: the second charm makes it sacrifice that
# one without being asked, and the Clue stays. Bot1's Mox Ruby and Mox Pearl each pay for one charm, untapping on turn 5.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Lorehold Charm
Lorehold Charm
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Thraben Inspector
Ornithopter
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lorehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Each opponent sacrifices)
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Thraben Inspector; Clue Token
? Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lorehold Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Each opponent sacrifices)
! Bot2.Choose
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Thraben Inspector; Clue Token
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 1
